ence and finish with the Black Joker. If the Queen is beaten by a King, Ace, or 2, I can use the Black Joker to regain control and then play the 77-88 sequence to win (assuming no bombs/Rocket). Passing would result in losing tempo and keeping a single Queen that is harder to play later.\n\nReason: The hand can be perfectly decomposed into a Pair Sequence (77-88), a single Q, and the Black Joker. The Q is the weakest part of this setup and should be played on the J to clear it. The Black Joker provides insurance to regain the lead and play the pair sequence.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥Q"]}'}
